Financial Data Validation & Portfolio Analytics Automation
Project Overview

This project automates an end-to-end financial data validation and portfolio analytics workflow using Python and SQL Server. The solution streamlines the ingestion of Excel-based financial datasets, executes SQL-based data quality validations, applies business rules, creates clean analytical datasets, and generates portfolio analytics for reporting and decision support.

The objective is to reduce manual effort, standardize data quality processes, and automate the execution of enterprise SQL workflows through Python.

Business Problem

Financial institutions receive security master, pricing, holdings, transactions, and FX data from multiple upstream systems. Manual validation and execution of SQL scripts are time-consuming, error-prone, and difficult to maintain.

The business requires an automated framework capable of:

Importing multiple datasets
Executing standardized SQL validations
Detecting data quality issues
Cleaning invalid records
Enforcing business rules
Creating analytical views
Supporting portfolio risk analysis
Solution

Developed a Python automation framework that orchestrates the complete SQL workflow, enabling repeatable and consistent execution of financial data quality checks and portfolio analytics.

